      "year": 2025,
      "abstract": "This article conducts a comparative analysis of the concepts of culture in Louis Althusser\u2019s structuralist Marxism and Theodor Adorno\u2019s critical theory from the Frankfurt School. Both traditions build on Marxist foundations but offer divergent interpretations of culture\u2019s role in capitalist society. Althusser views culture as part of the ideo-logical state apparatuses that reproduce social relations through the interpellation of subjects, whereas Adorno examines the \u201cculture industry\u201d as a mechanism of standardization and suppression of individuality, masking class contradictions. The study highlights key similarities (critique of ideology as a tool of domination) and dif-ferences (structural determinism vs. dialectical critique), emphasizing their conflict as a methodological dilem-ma for contemporary cultural studies, where combining the approaches enables analysis from institutional mechanisms to the psychological impact of culture.",
